{"id":"u164","kelas":"kosa","no":17,"judul":"Phrasal Verb Menengah 1: Kerja dan Belajar","title":"Phrasal Verbs: Work and Study","emoji":"🧷","ringkas":"look up, find out, carry out, set up, catch up, hand in","ready":true,"goals":["memahami **phrasal verb menengah** untuk kerja dan belajar","memakai phrasal verb dalam kalimat dengan **objek di tengah atau di belakang**","mengenali **arti yang berbeda** dari kata kerja dasarnya","membedakan phrasal verb yang **dapat dan tidak dapat dipisah**"],"lesson":[{"t":"intro","text":"Phrasal verb dasar sudah kamu pelajari di Kelas 7. Kini kita masuk ke phrasal verb menengah yang sering muncul di kantor dan kampus. Perhatikan: sebagian dapat dipisah (*look it up*), sebagian tidak (*look after children*)."},{"t":"vocab","title":"1. Belajar dan penelitian","items":[{"en":"look up","id":"mencari informasi","ex":"Please look up the word in a dictionary."},{"en":"find out","id":"mencari tahu","ex":"I need to find out the answer."},{"en":"carry out","id":"melaksanakan","ex":"Scientists carry out experiments."},{"en":"catch up","id":"mengejar ketertinggalan","ex":"I must catch up on my homework."},{"en":"hand in","id":"mengumpulkan","ex":"Hand in your essay on Friday."},{"en":"go over","id":"mengulas","ex":"Let's go over the lesson again."},{"en":"sum up","id":"meringkas","ex":"Can you sum up the story?"},{"en":"point out","id":"menunjukkan","ex":"The teacher pointed out my mistake."}]},{"t":"vocab","title":"2. Pekerjaan dan proyek","items":[{"en":"set up","id":"mendirikan / menyiapkan","ex":"They set up a new company."},{"en":"take on","id":"mengambil (tugas)","ex":"She took on extra work."},{"en":"deal with","id":"menangani","ex":"We deal with customers every day."},{"en":"work out","id":"menyelesaikan / menghitung","ex":"I cannot work out the answer."},{"en":"put off","id":"menunda","ex":"They put off the meeting until Monday."},{"en":"turn down","id":"menolak","ex":"He turned down the job offer."},{"en":"back up","id":"mencadangkan / mendukung","ex":"Please back up your files."},{"en":"fill in","id":"mengisi","ex":"Fill in this form, please."}]},{"t":"vocab","title":"3. Komunikasi dan rencana","items":[{"en":"get back to","id":"menghubungi kembali","ex":"I'll get back to you tomorrow."},{"en":"bring up","id":"mengemukakan","ex":"He brought up a good point."},{"en":"follow up","id":"menindaklanjuti","ex":"I will follow up with the client."},{"en":"run into","id":"bertemu tak sengaja","ex":"I ran into my old teacher."},{"en":"come up with","id":"menemukan (ide)","ex":"She came up with a clever plan."},{"en":"figure out","id":"memahami / memecahkan","ex":"We figured out the problem."},{"en":"look into","id":"menyelidiki","ex":"The manager will look into the matter."},{"en":"sign up","id":"mendaftar","ex":"Sign up for the course online."}]},{"t":"dialog","title":"Dialog: Mengejar tugas","lines":[{"who":"Tom","en":"Did you hand in the report?","id":"Apakah kamu sudah mengumpulkan laporan?"},{"who":"Dina","en":"Not yet. I need to catch up on the data first.","id":"Belum. Aku perlu mengejar data dulu."},{"who":"Tom","en":"Can I help you work it out?","id":"Bolehkah aku membantumu menyelesaikannya?"},{"who":"Dina","en":"Yes, please. Then I'll follow up with Mr. Adi.","id":"Ya, tolong. Lalu aku akan menindaklanjuti dengan Pak Adi."}]},{"t":"tip","title":"Cara menghafal","text":"Pecah phrasal verb menjadi dua bagian dan buat satu kalimat sendiri untuk setiap pasangan. Kata ganti selalu di tengah pada phrasal verb yang dapat dipisah: *look it up*, bukan *look up it*."},{"t":"summary","items":["Belajar dan penelitian: [[look up]], [[find out]], [[carry out]], [[catch up]], [[hand in]], [[go over]].","Pekerjaan dan proyek: [[set up]], [[take on]], [[deal with]], [[work out]], [[put off]], [[turn down]].","Komunikasi dan rencana: [[get back to]], [[bring up]], [[follow up]], [[run into]], [[come up with]], [[figure out]]."]}],"practice":[{"type":"mcq","q":"Apa arti \"look up\"?","options":["mencari inform